// Title: Proxy Execution Via Wuauclt.EXE
// ID: af77cf95-c469-471c-b6a0-946c685c4798
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: Roberto Rodriguez (Cyb3rWard0g), OTR (Open Threat Research), Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Sreeman, FPT.EagleEye Team
// Date: 2020-10-12
// Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1218, attack.execution
// Description: Detects the use of the Windows Update Client binary (wuauclt.exe) for proxy execution.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

process where ((((process.command_line like "*_UpdateDeploymentProvider*" and process.command_line like "*_RunHandlerComServer*")) and ((process.executable endswith "\\wuauclt.exe") or (process.pe.original_file_name == "wuauclt.exe"))) and not (((process.command_line like "*_ /UpdateDeploymentProvider UpdateDeploymentProvider.dll *") or ((process.command_line like "*_:\\Windows\\UUS\\Packages\\Preview\\amd64\\updatedeploy.dll /ClassId*" or process.command_line like "*_:\\Windows\\UUS\\amd64\\UpdateDeploy.dll /ClassId*")) or ((process.command_line like "*_:\\Windows\\WinSxS\\*" and process.command_line like "*_\\UpdateDeploy.dll /ClassId *")) or (process.command_line like "*_ wuaueng.dll *"))))
